         <p>Bereits vorhandene RP-Anfrageprotokolle können zusätzlich Absender- und Zielaccount, angefragten RP-Namen, Anfragezeitpunkt, Ergebnis, IP-Adresse und User-Agent enthalten. Änderungsprotokolle können den vorherigen und neuen RP-Namen enthalten. Diese Protokolle dienen der Nachvollziehbarkeit von Änderungen und der Untersuchung fehlerhafter oder missbräuchlicher Anfragen; sie werden nicht als öffentliches Namensarchiv bereitgestellt.</p>
         <p><strong>Aufbewahrung:</strong> Die serverseitige RP-Zuordnung wird sechs Kalendermonate ab ihrer letzten ausdrücklichen Bestätigung oder Aktualisierung aufbewahrt und anschließend beim regelmäßigen Bereinigungslauf entfernt. Reines Abrufen oder gewöhnliche Spieleraktivität verlängert diese Frist nicht. Für vorhandene Zuordnungen ohne belegbaren Zeitpunkt beginnt einmalig mit der Einführung der Bereinigung eine sechsmonatige Übergangsfrist. Änderungs- und RP-Anfrageprotokolle werden sechs Kalendermonate ab ihrem jeweiligen Eintrag aufbewahrt und danach bereinigt. Fehlende Protokollzeitpunkte erhalten ebenfalls einmalig eine sechsmonatige Übergangsfrist. Andere Spielerdaten werden durch diese RP-Namensbereinigung nicht gelöscht.</p>
         <p>Die sechs Monate schließen eine frühere Berichtigung oder eine nach den gesetzlichen Voraussetzungen erforderliche Löschung nicht aus. Auskunft, Berichtigung, Löschung und Widerspruch können beim Kontakt in Abschnitt 1 beantragt werden. Zur Zuordnung genügt zunächst die Minecraft-UUID oder der Accountname; bei Bedarf wird ein geeigneter Nachweis der Kontozugehörigkeit angefordert. Bitte keine Minecraft-, Microsoft- oder Discord-Passwörter senden.</p>
-        <p>Die serverseitige Bereinigung kann bereits abgerufene lokale Kopien auf Spielerrechnern nicht nachträglich entfernen. Lokale RP-Daten und selbst angelegte Exporte werden gesondert auf dem jeweiligen Gerät verwaltet. Die genannten Fristen beziehen sich auf den laufenden RP-Datenbestand und seine RP-Protokolle; Sicherungskopien müssen gesondert in die Aufbewahrungs- und Löschverwaltung einbezogen werden. Vor einer Wiederherstellung müssen bereits abgelaufene oder zu löschende RP-Daten erneut berücksichtigt werden.</p>
+        <p>Die serverseitige Bereinigung kann bereits abgerufene lokale Kopien auf Spielerrechnern nicht nachträglich entfernen. Lokale RP-Daten und selbst angelegte Exporte werden gesondert auf dem jeweiligen Gerät verwaltet. Für neu eingerichtete, verschlüsselte RP-Sicherungskopien gilt eine Aufbewahrung von 30 Tagen mit täglicher Bereinigung. Die Sicherungen enthalten nur RP-Zuordnungen, RP-Protokolle und gegebenenfalls Namensvorschläge. Sie sind getrennt vom öffentlichen Webverzeichnis gespeichert und nur für die Administration zugänglich. Diese Regel beschreibt keine noch ungeprüften zusätzlichen Sicherungen des Hosters oder manuell angelegten Kopien.</p>
+        <p>Nach einer erforderlichen Löschung oder einem akzeptierten Widerspruch kann eine minimale Sperrinformation gespeichert bleiben, um erneute Einträge durch Uploads, Imports oder die Wiederherstellung einer Datenbanksicherung zu verhindern. Sie enthält einen aus der Minecraft-UUID abgeleiteten Prüfwert und den Sperrstatus, keine gelöschten RP-Namen. Der Prüfwert ist nicht anonym. Die Sperre wird nur so lange benötigt, wie die weitere Verarbeitung verhindert werden muss; ihre Erforderlichkeit wird bei Änderungen und regelmäßig überprüft. Vor Wiederherstellungen werden der aktuelle Lösch-/Sperrstand und die ursprünglichen Ablaufdaten berücksichtigt.</p>
+        <p>Für eine spätere Freigabe ist vorgesehen: Angemeldete Minecraft-Nutzer können eigene RP-Namen bestätigen; Meldungen über andere Spieler werden zunächst als nichtöffentliche Vorschläge für die Administration gespeichert. Vorschläge enthalten Absender-UUID, Ziel-UUID, vorgeschlagenen Namen und Zeitpunkt und werden spätestens beim Bereinigungslauf nach sechs Kalendermonaten ohne erneute Aktualisierung entfernt. Eine Meldung überschreibt keinen bestätigten fremden Namen. Das automatische Teilen bleibt bis zur Klärung der oben genannten Voraussetzungen deaktiviert.</p>
 
         <h2>7. Kontaktaufnahme</h2>
         <p>Bei einer Kontaktaufnahme per E-Mail werden die übermittelten Angaben zur Bearbeitung der Anfrage verarbeitet. Rechtsgrundlage ist je nach Inhalt Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. b DSGVO oder Art. 6 Abs. 1 lit. f DSGVO. Die Daten werden gelöscht, sobald die Anfrage abschließend bearbeitet wurde und keine gesetzlichen Aufbewahrungspflichten oder berechtigten Gründe für eine weitere Speicherung bestehen.</p>
diff --git "a/OttoRegions Web/includes/rp_privacy.php" "b/OttoRegions Web/includes/rp_privacy.php"
--- /dev/null
+++ "b/OttoRegions Web/includes/rp_privacy.php"
@@ -0,0 +1,163 @@
+<?php
+declare(strict_types=1);
+
+/** Current deletion state is independent of database backups; HTTP access is denied. */
+function rpPrivacyFilePrefix(): string
+{
+    return "<?php http_response_code(404); exit; __halt_compiler();\n";
+}
+
+function rpPrivacyDirectory(): string
+{
+    return defined('OTTO_RP_STATE_DIR') ? OTTO_RP_STATE_DIR : dirname(__DIR__) . '/var/rp-private';
+}
+
+function rpPrivacyLock(bool $exclusive)
+{
+    $dir = rpPrivacyDirectory();
+    if (!is_dir($dir) || is_link($dir)) { throw new RuntimeException('RP privacy state unavailable'); }
+    $handle = fopen($dir . '/state.lock.php', $exclusive ? 'c+' : 'rb');
+    if (!$handle || !flock($handle, $exclusive ? LOCK_EX : LOCK_SH)) { throw new RuntimeException('RP privacy lock unavailable'); }
+    if ($exclusive) {
+        chmod($dir . '/state.lock.php', 0640);
+        if (fstat($handle)['size'] === 0) { fwrite($handle, rpPrivacyFilePrefix()); fflush($handle); }
+    }
+    return $handle;
+}
+
+function rpPrivacyState(): array
+{
+    $file = rpPrivacyDirectory() . '/state.php';
+    if (!is_file($file) || is_link($file) || filesize($file) > 8 * 1024 * 1024) { throw new RuntimeException('RP privacy state unavailable'); }
+    $raw = (string) file_get_contents($file);
+    $prefix = rpPrivacyFilePrefix();
+    if (!str_starts_with($raw, $prefix)) { throw new RuntimeException('Invalid private PHP envelope'); }
+    $state = json_decode(substr($raw, strlen($prefix)), true, 32, JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR);
+    if (($state['version'] ?? null) !== 1 || !is_array($state['blocked'] ?? null)
+        || !is_bool($state['maintenance'] ?? null) || !is_bool($state['uploads_enabled'] ?? null)
+        || !preg_match('/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{2}$/D', $state['migration_started_at'] ?? '')) {
+        throw new RuntimeException('Invalid RP privacy state');
+    }
+    foreach ($state['blocked'] as $hash => $blocked) {
+        if (!preg_match('/^[a-f0-9]{64}$/D', $hash) || $blocked !== true) { throw new RuntimeException('Invalid RP suppression'); }
+    }
+    return $state;
+}
+
+/** Caller must hold the exclusive state.lock. Atomic replacement keeps corrupt writes closed. */
+function rpPrivacySave(array $state): void
+{
+    $path = rpPrivacyDirectory() . '/state.php';
+    $tmp = $path . '.' . bin2hex(random_bytes(8)) . '.tmp.php';
+    try {
+        $bytes = rpPrivacyFilePrefix() . json_encode($state, JSON_PRETTY_PRINT | JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR);
+        if (file_put_contents($tmp, $bytes, LOCK_EX) !== strlen($bytes)) { throw new RuntimeException('RP state write failed'); }
+        // Keep the deployment's narrowly assigned PHP read ACL effective.
+        chmod($tmp, 0640);
+        if (!rename($tmp, $path)) { throw new RuntimeException('RP state replacement failed'); }
+    } finally { if (is_file($tmp)) { unlink($tmp); } }
+}
+
+function rpPrivacyInitialize(string $migrationStart): void
+{
+    if (!preg_match('/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{2}$/D', $migrationStart)) { throw new InvalidArgumentException('UTC migration time required'); }
+    $dir = rpPrivacyDirectory();
+    if (is_link($dir)) { throw new RuntimeException('Private RP directory cannot be a symlink'); }
+    if (!is_dir($dir) && !mkdir($dir, 0700, true)) { throw new RuntimeException('Cannot create private RP directory'); }
+    $lock = rpPrivacyLock(true);
+    try {
+        if (file_exists($dir . '/state.php')) { rpPrivacyState(); return; }
+        rpPrivacySave(['version' => 1, 'migration_started_at' => $migrationStart,
+            'maintenance' => false, 'uploads_enabled' => false, 'blocked' => new stdClass()]);
+    } finally { flock($lock, LOCK_UN); fclose($lock); }
+}
+
+/** Hold for the whole request/sync: deletion and restore cannot interleave with publication. */
+function rpPrivacyHoldRead(): array
+{
+    if (empty($GLOBALS['rp_privacy_exclusive']) && empty($GLOBALS['rp_privacy_read_lock'])) {
+        $GLOBALS['rp_privacy_read_lock'] = rpPrivacyLock(false);
+    }
+    $state = rpPrivacyState();
+    if ($state['maintenance']) { throw new RuntimeException('RP privacy maintenance'); }
+    return $state;
+}
+
+function rpPrivacyReleaseRead(): void
+{
+    if (!empty($GLOBALS['rp_privacy_read_lock'])) {
+        flock($GLOBALS['rp_privacy_read_lock'], LOCK_UN);
+        fclose($GLOBALS['rp_privacy_read_lock']);
+        unset($GLOBALS['rp_privacy_read_lock']);
+    }
+}
+
+function rpPrivacyUuid(string $uuid): ?string
+{
+    $uuid = strtolower(str_replace('-', '', trim($uuid)));
+    return preg_match('/^[a-f0-9]{32}$/D', $uuid) ? $uuid : null;
+}
+
+function rpPrivacyBlocked(string $uuid, ?array $state = null): bool
+{
+    $normalized = rpPrivacyUuid($uuid);
+    return $normalized === null || isset(($state ?? rpPrivacyState())['blocked'][hash('sha256', $normalized)]);
+}
+
+/** Delete only RP data, including logs identifying the affected actor or target. */
+function rpPrivacyPurgeBlocked(PDO $pdo, array $state): void
+{
+    foreach (array_keys($state['blocked']) as $hash) {
+        $accounts = $pdo->prepare("SELECT entity_key, name FROM external_participants WHERE SHA2(REPLACE(LOWER(uuid), '-', ''), 256) = ?");
+        $accounts->execute([$hash]);
+        $identities = $accounts->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);
+        $pdo->prepare("UPDATE external_participants SET rp_name = NULL, rp_name_expires_at = NULL, rp_name_source = 'legacy'
+            WHERE SHA2(REPLACE(LOWER(uuid), '-', ''), 256) = ?")->execute([$hash]);
+        foreach (['external_participant_rp_name_log', 'external_participant_rp_name_request_log', 'rp_name_proposals'] as $table) {
+            if (!rpNameTableExists($pdo, $table)) { continue; }
+            $pdo->prepare("DELETE FROM {$table} WHERE SHA2(REPLACE(LOWER(actor_uuid), '-', ''), 256) = ?
+                OR SHA2(REPLACE(LOWER(target_uuid), '-', ''), 256) = ?")->execute([$hash, $hash]);
+            if ($table !== 'rp_name_proposals') {
+                $columns = $pdo->query('SHOW COLUMNS FROM ' . $table)->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_COLUMN);
+                foreach ($identities as $identity) {
+                    foreach (['actor_name', 'target_name', 'actor_entity_key', 'target_entity_key', 'resolved_actor_entity_key', 'resolved_target_entity_key'] as $column) {
+                        $value = str_ends_with($column, '_name') ? $identity['name'] : $identity['entity_key'];
+                        if ($value !== '' && $value !== null && in_array($column, $columns, true)) {
+                            $pdo->prepare("DELETE FROM {$table} WHERE `{$column}` = ?")->execute([$value]);
+                        }
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/** Exclusive, recoverable operation: failures keep publication closed. */
+function rpPrivacyManage(PDO $pdo, string $operation, ?string $uuid = null): array
+{
+    if ($pdo->inTransaction() || !empty($GLOBALS['rp_privacy_read_lock'])) { throw new LogicException('Privacy management needs an independent connection'); }
+    if (!in_array($operation, ['block', 'unblock', 'restore-begin', 'restore-finish'], true)) { throw new InvalidArgumentException('Unknown privacy operation'); }
+    if (in_array($operation, ['block', 'unblock'], true) && rpPrivacyUuid((string) $uuid) === null) { throw new InvalidArgumentException('UUID required'); }
+    $lock = rpPrivacyLock(true);
+    $GLOBALS['rp_privacy_exclusive'] = true;
+    try {
+        $state = rpPrivacyState();
+        $wasMaintenance = $state['maintenance'];
+        $state['maintenance'] = true;
+        if ($operation === 'block') { $state['blocked'][hash('sha256', rpPrivacyUuid($uuid))] = true; }
+        if ($operation === 'unblock') { unset($state['blocked'][hash('sha256', rpPrivacyUuid($uuid))]); }
+        rpPrivacySave($state);
+        if ($operation !== 'restore-begin') {
+            rpNameEnsureRetentionSchema($pdo);
+            $pdo->beginTransaction();
+            try { rpPrivacyPurgeBlocked($pdo, $state); $pdo->commit(); }
+            catch (Throwable $e) { if ($pdo->inTransaction()) { $pdo->rollBack(); } throw $e; }
+            $cleanup = rpNameCleanup($pdo, true);
+            if (array_sum($cleanup['remaining']) !== 0) { throw new RuntimeException('Cleanup incomplete; maintenance remains active'); }
+            // A block/unblock must not accidentally finish an existing restore.
+            $state['maintenance'] = $operation === 'restore-finish' ? false : $wasMaintenance;
+            rpPrivacySave($state);
+        }
+        return ['ok' => true, 'maintenance' => $state['maintenance'], 'blocked_count' => count($state['blocked'])];
+    } finally { unset($GLOBALS['rp_privacy_exclusive']); flock($lock, LOCK_UN); fclose($lock); }
+}
diff --git "a/OttoRegions Web/includes/rp_name_upload.php" "b/OttoRegions Web/includes/rp_name_upload.php"
--- /dev/null
+++ "b/OttoRegions Web/includes/rp_name_upload.php"
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+<?php
+declare(strict_types=1);
+require_once __DIR__ . '/rp_name_retention.php';
+require_once __DIR__ . '/v2/auth.php';
+require_once __DIR__ . '/v2/security.php';
+
+/** The same tested entry point is used by the HTTP route and isolated integration tests. */
+function rpNameHandleUpload(PDO $pdo, ?string $authorization, string $raw, string $ip): array
+{
+    $state = rpPrivacyHoldRead();
+    $auth = v2ValidateJwt($pdo, $authorization);
+    if (!$auth['ok']) { return [(int) $auth['status'], ['ok' => false, 'error' => $auth['error']]]; }
+    $auth['uuid'] = rpPrivacyUuid($auth['uuid']);
+    if (!$state['uploads_enabled']) { return [503, ['ok' => false, 'error' => 'rp_uploads_unavailable']]; }
+    foreach ([['ip:' . hash('sha256', $ip), 120], ['uuid:' . $auth['uuid'], 30]] as [$key, $limit]) {
+        if (!v2RateLimitHit($pdo, 'rp-names', $key, $limit, 60)['allowed']) {
+            return [429, ['ok' => false, 'error' => 'rate_limited']];
+        }
+    }
+    if (strlen($raw) > 2048) { return [413, ['ok' => false, 'error' => 'payload_too_large']]; }
+    try { $body = json_decode($raw, true, 8, JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR); }
+    catch (JsonException $e) { return [400, ['ok' => false, 'error' => 'invalid_json']]; }
+    if (!is_array($body) || array_diff(array_keys($body), ['target_uuid', 'target_player_name', 'rp_name'])
+        || !is_string($body['rp_name'] ?? null)) { return [422, ['ok' => false, 'error' => 'invalid_fields']]; }
+    $name = trim($body['rp_name']);
+    if ($name === '' || !mb_check_encoding($name, 'UTF-8') || mb_strlen($name, 'UTF-8') > 120
+        || preg_match('/[\p{C}<>]/u', $name)) { return [422, ['ok' => false, 'error' => 'invalid_rp_name']]; }
+    $targetUuid = isset($body['target_uuid']) && is_string($body['target_uuid']) ? rpPrivacyUuid($body['target_uuid']) : null;
+    $targetName = $body['target_player_name'] ?? null;
+    if ((isset($body['target_uuid']) && $targetUuid === null)
+        || ($targetName !== null && (!is_string($targetName) || !preg_match('/^[A-Za-z0-9_]{3,16}$/D', $targetName)))) {
+        return [422, ['ok' => false, 'error' => 'invalid_target']];
+    }
+    if ($targetUuid === null && $targetName === null) { $targetUuid = $auth['uuid']; }
+    $query = $targetUuid !== null ? "REPLACE(LOWER(uuid), '-', '') = :target" : 'LOWER(name) = LOWER(:target)';
+    $stmt = $pdo->prepare('SELECT entity_key, uuid, name, rp_name FROM external_participants WHERE ' . $query . ' LIMIT 2');
+    $stmt->execute([':target' => $targetUuid ?? $targetName]);
+    $rows = $stmt->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);
+    if (count($rows) !== 1) { return [404, ['ok' => false, 'error' => 'target_not_unique']]; }
+    $target = $rows[0];
+    if ($targetName !== null && strcasecmp($targetName, (string) $target['name']) !== 0) { return [422, ['ok' => false, 'error' => 'target_mismatch']]; }
+    if (rpPrivacyBlocked($auth['uuid'], $state) || rpPrivacyBlocked((string) $target['uuid'], $state)) {
+        return [403, ['ok' => false, 'error' => 'rp_processing_blocked']];
+    }
+    $targetId = rpPrivacyUuid($target['uuid']);
+    if ($targetId === $auth['uuid']) {
+        rpNameStore($pdo, $target['entity_key'], $name, 'self');
+        return [200, ['ok' => true, 'message' => 'Eigener RP-Name bestaetigt.']];
+    }
+    // A logged-in observer cannot prove another player's identity; queue privately.
+    $stmt = $pdo->prepare('INSERT INTO rp_name_proposals (actor_uuid, target_uuid, rp_name, created_at)
+        VALUES (?, ?, ?, UTC_TIMESTAMP()) ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE rp_name = VALUES(rp_name), created_at = UTC_TIMESTAMP()');
+    $stmt->execute([$auth['uuid'], $targetId, $name]);
+    return [202, ['ok' => true, 'message' => 'Namensvorschlag zur Pruefung gespeichert.']];
+}
diff --git "a/OttoRegions Web/includes/rp_backups.php" "b/OttoRegions Web/includes/rp_backups.php"
--- /dev/null
+++ "b/OttoRegions Web/includes/rp_backups.php"
@@ -0,0 +1,227 @@
+<?php
+declare(strict_types=1);
+require_once __DIR__ . '/rp_name_retention.php';
+
+function rpBackupRoot(): string
+{
+    return defined('OTTO_RP_STATE_DIR') ? OTTO_RP_STATE_DIR : dirname(__DIR__, 2) . '/ottoextra-rp-private';
+}
+
+function rpBackupBufferedAttribute(): int
+{
+    return defined('Pdo\\Mysql::ATTR_USE_BUFFERED_QUERY')
+        ? constant('Pdo\\Mysql::ATTR_USE_BUFFERED_QUERY') : constant('PDO::MYSQL_ATTR_USE_BUFFERED_QUERY');
+}
+
+function rpBackupTables(): array
+{
+    return ['external_participant_rp_name_log', 'external_participant_rp_name_request_log', 'rp_name_proposals'];
+}
+
+function rpBackupKey(): string
+{
+    $path = rpBackupRoot() . '/backup.key';
+    if (!is_file($path) || is_link($path)) { throw new RuntimeException('RP backup key unavailable'); }
+    $key = file_get_contents($path);
+    if (strlen($key) !== SODIUM_CRYPTO_SECRETBOX_KEYBYTES) { throw new RuntimeException('Invalid RP backup key'); }
+    return $key;
+}
+
+function rpBackupInitialize(): void
+{
+    $lock = rpPrivacyLock(true);
+    try {
+        rpPrivacyState();
+        $root = rpBackupRoot();
+        if (!is_dir($root) && !mkdir($root, 0700, true)) { throw new RuntimeException('Cannot create private backup root'); }
+        $dir = $root . '/backups';
+        if (!is_dir($dir) && !mkdir($dir, 0700)) { throw new RuntimeException('Cannot create RP backup directory'); }
+        if (is_link($dir)) { throw new RuntimeException('Backup symlink rejected'); }
+        if (!file_exists($root . '/backup.key')) {
+            $f = fopen($root . '/backup.key', 'xb');
+            if (!$f) { throw new RuntimeException('Cannot initialize backup key'); }
+            chmod($root . '/backup.key', 0600);
+            try { if (fwrite($f, random_bytes(SODIUM_CRYPTO_SECRETBOX_KEYBYTES)) !== SODIUM_CRYPTO_SECRETBOX_KEYBYTES) { throw new RuntimeException('Key write failed'); } }
+            finally { fclose($f); }
+        }
+        rpBackupKey();
+    } finally { flock($lock, LOCK_UN); fclose($lock); }
+}
+
+function rpBackupFile(string $name): string
+{
+    if (!preg_match('/^rp-backup-(\d{8}T\d{6}Z)-[a-f0-9]{16}\.box$/D', $name)) { throw new InvalidArgumentException('Managed RP backup filename required'); }
+    $dir = rpBackupRoot() . '/backups';
+    if (!is_dir($dir) || is_link($dir)) { throw new RuntimeException('Backup directory unavailable'); }
+    $file = $dir . '/' . $name;
+    if (is_link($file)) { throw new RuntimeException('Backup symlink rejected'); }
+    return $file;
+}
+
+function rpBackupRotate(bool $apply, ?int $now = null): array
+{
+    $now ??= time();
+    $eligible = [];
+    foreach (new DirectoryIterator(rpBackupRoot() . '/backups') as $entry) {
+        if (!$entry->isFile() || $entry->isLink()) { continue; }
+        $name = $entry->getFilename();
+        if (!preg_match('/^rp-backup-(\d{8}T\d{6}Z)-[a-f0-9]{16}\.box$/D', $name, $m)) { continue; }
+        $date = DateTimeImmutable::createFromFormat('!Ymd\THis\Z', $m[1], new DateTimeZone('UTC'));
+        if (!$date || $date->format('Ymd\THis\Z') !== $m[1]) { continue; }
+        if ($date->getTimestamp() + 30 * 86400 <= $now) {
+            $eligible[] = $name;
+            if ($apply && !unlink(rpBackupFile($name))) { throw new RuntimeException('Backup rotation failed'); }
+        }
+    }
+    return ['eligible' => count($eligible), 'deleted' => $apply ? count($eligible) : 0];
+}
+
+/** Stream encrypted rows; memory is bounded by one record, not the database size. */
+function rpBackupCreate(PDO $pdo): array
+{
+    rpPrivacyHoldRead();
+    if ($pdo->inTransaction()) { throw new LogicException('Backup requires an independent connection'); }
+    $rotation = rpBackupRotate(true);
+    $key = rpBackupKey();
+    [$cipherState, $header] = sodium_crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_init_push($key);
+    $name = 'rp-backup-' . gmdate('Ymd\THis\Z') . '-' . bin2hex(random_bytes(8)) . '.box';
+    $file = rpBackupFile($name);
+    $f = fopen($file, 'xb');
+    if (!$f) { throw new RuntimeException('Cannot create RP backup'); }
+    chmod($file, 0600);
+    $write = static function (string $bytes) use ($f): void {
+        while ($bytes !== '') {
+            $n = fwrite($f, $bytes);
+            if ($n === false || $n === 0) { throw new RuntimeException('Incomplete RP backup'); }
+            $bytes = substr($bytes, $n);
+        }
+    };
+    $frame = static function (array $value, bool $final = false) use (&$cipherState, $write): void {
+        $plain = json_encode($value, JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR);
+        if (strlen($plain) > 16 * 1024 * 1024) { throw new RuntimeException('RP backup record exceeds 16 MiB'); }
+        $encrypted = sodium_crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_push($cipherState, $plain, '', $final
+            ? SODIUM_CRYPTO_SECRETSTREAM_XCHACHA20POLY1305_TAG_FINAL : SODIUM_CRYPTO_SECRETSTREAM_XCHACHA20POLY1305_TAG_MESSAGE);
+        $write(pack('N', strlen($encrypted)) . $encrypted);
+    };
+    $sessionZone = (string) $pdo->query('SELECT @@session.time_zone')->fetchColumn();
+    $buffered = $pdo->getAttribute(rpBackupBufferedAttribute());
+    $completed = false;
+    $rows = 0;
+    try {
+        $write("OERP2\n" . $header);
+        $frame(['version' => 2, 'created_at' => gmdate('c'), 'tables' => array_merge(['external_participants'], rpBackupTables())]);
+        $pdo->exec("SET time_zone = '+00:00'");
+        $pdo->setAttribute(rpBackupBufferedAttribute(), false);
+        $pdo->beginTransaction();
+        $queries = ['external_participants' => 'SELECT entity_key, uuid, rp_name, rp_name_expires_at, rp_name_source FROM external_participants WHERE rp_name IS NOT NULL'];
+        foreach (rpBackupTables() as $table) { $queries[$table] = 'SELECT * FROM ' . $table; }
+        foreach ($queries as $table => $sql) {
+            if (!rpNameTableExists($pdo, $table)) { continue; }
+            $stmt = $pdo->query($sql);
+            try {
+                while ($row = $stmt->fetch(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC)) { $frame(['table' => $table, 'row' => $row]); $rows++; }
+            } finally { $stmt->closeCursor(); }
+        }
+        $pdo->commit();
+        $frame(['end' => true, 'rows' => $rows], true);
+        fflush($f); fclose($f); $f = null;
+        foreach (rpBackupRecords($name) as $_) { } // Complete authentication, including final marker.
+        $completed = true;
+        return ['file' => $name, 'bytes' => filesize($file), 'rows' => $rows, 'rotation' => $rotation];
+    } finally {
+        if ($pdo->inTransaction()) { $pdo->rollBack(); }
+        $pdo->setAttribute(rpBackupBufferedAttribute(), $buffered);
+        $pdo->exec('SET time_zone = ' . $pdo->quote($sessionZone));
+        if (is_resource($f)) { fclose($f); }
+        if (!$completed && is_file($file)) { unlink($file); }
+    }
+}
+
+/** Authenticate ordered records and require a final marker; rejects truncation and concatenation. */
+function rpBackupRecords(string $name): Generator
+{
+    $file = rpBackupFile($name);
+    if (!is_file($file)) { throw new RuntimeException('Backup unavailable'); }
+    $f = fopen($file, 'rb');
+    if (!$f) { throw new RuntimeException('Backup unavailable'); }
+    $read = static function (int $n) use ($f): string {
+        $bytes = '';
+        while (strlen($bytes) < $n) {
+            $part = fread($f, $n - strlen($bytes));
+            if ($part === false || $part === '') { throw new RuntimeException('Truncated RP backup'); }
+            $bytes .= $part;
+        }
+        return $bytes;
+    };
+    try {
+        if ($read(6) !== "OERP2\n") { throw new RuntimeException('Unsupported RP backup format'); }
+        $state = sodium_crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_init_pull($read(SODIUM_CRYPTO_SECRETSTREAM_XCHACHA20POLY1305_HEADERBYTES), rpBackupKey());
+        $first = true; $rows = 0;
+        while (true) {
+            $length = unpack('Nlength', $read(4))['length'];
+            if ($length < 17 || $length > 16 * 1024 * 1024 + 17) { throw new RuntimeException('Invalid RP backup frame'); }
+            $result = sodium_crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_pull($state, $read($length));
+            if ($result === false) { throw new RuntimeException('Backup authentication failed'); }
+            [$plain, $tag] = $result;
+            $value = json_decode($plain, true, 32, JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR);
+            if ($first) {
+                if (($value['version'] ?? null) !== 2 || ($value['tables'] ?? null) !== array_merge(['external_participants'], rpBackupTables())
+                    || $tag !== SODIUM_CRYPTO_SECRETSTREAM_XCHACHA20POLY1305_TAG_MESSAGE) { throw new RuntimeException('Invalid backup schema'); }
+                $first = false; continue;
+            }
+            if ($tag === SODIUM_CRYPTO_SECRETSTREAM_XCHACHA20POLY1305_TAG_FINAL) {
+                if (($value['end'] ?? null) !== true || ($value['rows'] ?? null) !== $rows || fread($f, 1) !== '') { throw new RuntimeException('Invalid final backup marker'); }
+                return;
+            }
+            if ($tag !== SODIUM_CRYPTO_SECRETSTREAM_XCHACHA20POLY1305_TAG_MESSAGE || !in_array($value['table'] ?? null, array_merge(['external_participants'], rpBackupTables()), true)
+                || !is_array($value['row'] ?? null)) { throw new RuntimeException('Invalid backup record'); }
+            $rows++; yield $value;
+        }
+    } finally { fclose($f); }
+}
+
+function rpBackupRestore(PDO $pdo, string $name): array
+{
+    foreach (rpBackupRecords($name) as $_) { } // Authenticate the whole stream before maintenance.
+    if ($pdo->inTransaction() || !empty($GLOBALS['rp_privacy_read_lock'])) { throw new LogicException('Restore requires an independent connection'); }
+    $lock = rpPrivacyLock(true); $GLOBALS['rp_privacy_exclusive'] = true;
+    $sessionZone = (string) $pdo->query('SELECT @@session.time_zone')->fetchColumn();
+    try {
+        $pdo->exec("SET time_zone = '+00:00'");
+        $state = rpPrivacyState(); $state['maintenance'] = true; rpPrivacySave($state);
+        rpNameEnsureRetentionSchema($pdo);
+        $pdo->beginTransaction();
+        try {
+            $pdo->exec("UPDATE external_participants SET rp_name = NULL, rp_name_expires_at = NULL, rp_name_source = 'legacy'");
+            $update = $pdo->prepare("UPDATE external_participants SET rp_name = ?, rp_name_expires_at = ?, rp_name_source = ?
+                WHERE entity_key = ? AND REPLACE(LOWER(uuid), '-', '') = ?");
+            $columns = [];
+            foreach (rpBackupTables() as $table) {
+                if (!rpNameTableExists($pdo, $table)) { continue; }
+                $pdo->exec('DELETE FROM ' . $table);
+                $columns[$table] = $pdo->query('SHOW COLUMNS FROM ' . $table)->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_COLUMN);
+            }
+            foreach (rpBackupRecords($name) as $record) {
+                $table = $record['table']; $row = $record['row'];
+                if ($table === 'external_participants') {
+                    if (rpPrivacyBlocked((string) ($row['uuid'] ?? ''), $state)) { continue; }
+                    $update->execute([$row['rp_name'], $row['rp_name_expires_at'], $row['rp_name_source'], $row['entity_key'], rpPrivacyUuid($row['uuid'])]);
+                } elseif (isset($columns[$table])) {
+                    $row = array_intersect_key($row, array_flip($columns[$table]));
+                    $cols = array_keys($row);
+                    if (!$cols) { continue; }
+                    $pdo->prepare('INSERT INTO ' . $table . ' (`' . implode('`,`', $cols) . '`) VALUES (' . implode(',', array_fill(0, count($cols), '?')) . ')')->execute(array_values($row));
+                }
+            }
+            rpPrivacyPurgeBlocked($pdo, $state);
+            $pdo->commit();
+        } catch (Throwable $e) { if ($pdo->inTransaction()) { $pdo->rollBack(); } throw $e; }
+        $cleanup = rpNameCleanup($pdo, true);
+        if (array_sum($cleanup['remaining']) !== 0) { throw new RuntimeException('Restore cleanup incomplete; maintenance remains active'); }
+        $state['maintenance'] = false; rpPrivacySave($state);
+        return ['ok' => true, 'maintenance' => false, 'cleanup' => $cleanup];
+    } finally {
+        unset($GLOBALS['rp_privacy_exclusive']); flock($lock, LOCK_UN); fclose($lock);
+        $pdo->exec('SET time_zone = ' . $pdo->quote($sessionZone));
+    }
+}
diff --git "a/OttoRegions Web/tools/rp-privacy.php" "b/OttoRegions Web/tools/rp-privacy.php"
--- /dev/null
+++ "b/OttoRegions Web/tools/rp-privacy.php"
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+<?php
+declare(strict_types=1);
+if (PHP_SAPI !== 'cli') { http_response_code(404); exit; }
+require_once __DIR__ . '/../includes/rp_backups.php';
+$args = array_slice($argv, 1);
+$operation = array_shift($args) ?? 'status';
+$apply = in_array('--apply', $args, true);
+$values = array_values(array_filter($args, static fn($arg) => $arg !== '--apply'));
+try {
+    if (!in_array($operation, ['status', 'init', 'block', 'unblock', 'restore-begin', 'restore-finish', 'backup', 'rotate', 'restore', 'proposals', 'approve-proposal', 'reject-proposal'], true)) { throw new InvalidArgumentException('Unknown operation'); }
+    $needsValue = in_array($operation, ['init', 'block', 'unblock', 'restore'], true);
+    $proposalChange = in_array($operation, ['approve-proposal', 'reject-proposal'], true);
+    if (count($values) !== ($proposalChange ? 2 : ($needsValue ? 1 : 0))) { throw new InvalidArgumentException('Unexpected arguments'); }
+    if ($operation === 'init') {
+        if (!$apply) { throw new InvalidArgumentException('init requires UTC timestamp and --apply'); }
+        rpPrivacyInitialize($values[0]); rpBackupInitialize();
+        echo json_encode(['ok' => true, 'initialized' => true]) . PHP_EOL; exit;
+    }
+    if ($operation === 'status') {
+        $lock = rpPrivacyLock(false);
+        try { $s = rpPrivacyState(); echo json_encode(['maintenance' => $s['maintenance'], 'uploads_enabled' => $s['uploads_enabled'], 'blocked_count' => count($s['blocked']), 'migration_started_at' => $s['migration_started_at']]) . PHP_EOL; }
+        finally { flock($lock, LOCK_UN); fclose($lock); }
+        exit;
+    }
+    if ($operation === 'rotate') {
+        $lock = rpPrivacyLock(true);
+        try { echo json_encode(rpBackupRotate($apply)) . PHP_EOL; }
+        finally { flock($lock, LOCK_UN); fclose($lock); }
+        exit;
+    }
+    if (!$apply && $operation !== 'proposals') { throw new InvalidArgumentException('This operation requires --apply'); }
+    require_once __DIR__ . '/../includes/bootstrap.php';
+    if (!$pdo instanceof PDO) { throw new RuntimeException('Database unavailable'); }
+    if ($operation === 'proposals') {
+        rpPrivacyHoldRead();
+        echo json_encode($pdo->query('SELECT actor_uuid, target_uuid, rp_name, created_at FROM rp_name_proposals ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 200')->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC), JSON_PRETTY_PRINT | JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR) . PHP_EOL; exit;
+    }
+    if ($proposalChange) {
+        rpPrivacyHoldRead();
+        $actor = rpPrivacyUuid($values[0]); $target = rpPrivacyUuid($values[1]);
+        if ($actor === null || $target === null) { throw new InvalidArgumentException('Actor and target UUID required'); }
+        $pdo->beginTransaction();
+        try {
+            $query = $pdo->prepare('SELECT rp_name FROM rp_name_proposals WHERE actor_uuid = ? AND target_uuid = ? FOR UPDATE');
+            $query->execute([$actor, $target]); $name = $query->fetchColumn();
+            if ($name === false) { throw new RuntimeException('Proposal not found'); }
+            if ($operation === 'approve-proposal') {
+                $find = $pdo->prepare("SELECT entity_key FROM external_participants WHERE REPLACE(LOWER(uuid), '-', '') = ? LIMIT 2");
+                $find->execute([$target]); $keys = $find->fetchAll(PDO::FETCH_COLUMN);
+                if (count($keys) !== 1) { throw new RuntimeException('Target is not unique'); }
+                rpNameStore($pdo, $keys[0], $name);
+            }
+            $pdo->prepare('DELETE FROM rp_name_proposals WHERE actor_uuid = ? AND target_uuid = ?')->execute([$actor, $target]);
+            $pdo->commit();
+        } catch (Throwable $e) { if ($pdo->inTransaction()) { $pdo->rollBack(); } throw $e; }
+        echo json_encode(['ok' => true, 'operation' => $operation]) . PHP_EOL; exit;
+    }
+    $result = match ($operation) {
+        'backup' => rpBackupCreate($pdo),
+        'restore' => rpBackupRestore($pdo, $values[0]),
+        default => rpPrivacyManage($pdo, $operation, $values[0] ?? null),
+    };
+    echo json_encode($result, JSON_PRETTY_PRINT | JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR) . PHP_EOL;
+} catch (Throwable $e) {
+    fwrite(STDERR, 'RP privacy operation failed: ' . $e->getMessage() . PHP_EOL); exit(1);
+}
